 ## Overview
 GaussianObject reconstructs 3D Gaussian Splatting representations from sparse or partial inputs by initializing Gaussians with a visual hull and fine-tuning a pre-trained ControlNet to repair degraded rendered images generated by adding noise to each Gaussian's attributes [S1, unofficial]. It outperforms previous NeRF-based sparse-view reconstruction methods [S1, unofficial].
-
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs:** Not given in the sources.
-**Data Structures:** Not given in the sources.
 **Steps:**
-1. Initialize 3D Gaussians with the visual hull derived from the input views.
-2. Add noise to each Gaussian's attributes to generate degraded rendered images.
-3. Fine-tune a pre-trained ControlNet to repair the degraded rendered images.
-4. Update the Gaussian attributes using the repaired outputs from the ControlNet.
